# Debugging

Do not guess. Investigate.

- Read the full error and stack trace. Do not patch from the error type alone.
- Reproduce before changing anything. If you cannot reproduce, you cannot verify a fix.
- Change one thing at a time. Test after each change.
- Do not add null checks or workarounds without finding why the value is wrong.
- If stuck after X and Y, say so with what you observed. Do not silently try random fixes for 20 iterations.
